```

Exact helper output:

```text
Error: failed to create a fresh ChatGPT Web worker tab

Caused by:
    command orca ["--json", "new-surface", "--type", "browser", "--url", "https://chatgpt.com", "--focus", "false"] failed (exit status: 1): {
      "id": "local",
      "ok": false,
      "error": {
        "code": "invalid_argument",
        "message": "Unknown command: new-surface false",
        "data": {
          "suggestions": [],
          "nextSteps": []
        }
      },
      "_meta": {
        "runtimeId": null
      }
    } 


Command exited with code 1
```

No scope IDs exist to retain because failure occurred before worker creation. I did not retry, since the task required exactly one fresh batch invocation and instructed stopping at the first authoritative terminal failure. Final cargo/frontend verification was not run because it was explicitly gated on both workers finishing.
